        "parms": "# sprintf — build a message from a format\nsprintf fills the placeholders in a format: %d for an int, %f for a float, %s for a word and %c for a character code. Each placeholder has its own inlet. The left one formats and sends, the others only store.\nUnlike Max's sprintf, the result always leaves as text, so symout changes nothing. Only %d, %i, %f, %s, %c and %% are understood: %x, %g and the like are copied through as text.",
